+# Review applyPatch conformance to RFC 6902
+
+Reviewed validation and application of `applyPatch` against RFC 6902 (operations, pointer handling,
+array indices, `-`, move prefix rule, test equality, atomic failure). Two deviations found and fixed in
+`src/index.ts`:
+
+- A sparse patch array (holes) was accepted as if the holes were absent; `Array.from` now visits every
+  slot, so a hole is rejected as an invalid operation.
+- `move` from the root onto the root threw "whole document cannot be removed"; moving a value onto
+  itself is now a no-op for every path, as dl-002 states.
+
+Tests added in `test/patch.test.ts`; `npm test` passes (38). The rest was verified conformant. Decision: dl-003.
